  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "when i load into my world upon starting vrchat,  its set as my home world, it takes me a solid 45seconds to a minute before i can click anything and go inside the buildings or whatever else in the map.\n\nThen if i host it publicly, everyone else seems to have the same issue, they get stuck in the air at spawn even though they are moving around the map, then after a solid minute they pop into place and it goes normally. However this applies to only them. When i join, i cant ever get past that state. I stay, to everyone elses viewpoint, suspended in midair at spawn, while on my screen i move around. Ive waited 15 minutes before and i still hadnt loaded in for anyone, i stayed stuck in the air while on my screen i desperately tried hugging them....its really sad. its like im a ghost. If i pick up an object they can see it move. But ya, it never used to do this and idk why when i join or host one instance that isnt my private home world, i become stuck forever for everyone else.\n\nCurrently world is still public.\n\nWorld id is wrld_bcf35b2c-1f04-49cc-b944-ee127c37a7ed\n\nWorld has newest SDK, and world used to work PERFECTLY before the update around April 10th.\n\nMade a previous post about that update and the issues here: https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/746-menu-does-not-appear-when-using-steam-in-certain-worlds-using-desktop-or-ocu\n\ncould be a continuation.",
